  "interpretation": "<p>Factor IX is a <strong data-start=\"98\" data-end=\"137\">vitamin K&ndash;dependent clotting factor</strong>, also known as <strong data-start=\"153\" data-end=\"173\">Christmas factor</strong>. It plays a crucial role in the <strong data-start=\"206\" data-end=\"227\">intrinsic pathway</strong> of the coagulation cascade. The <strong data-start=\"260\" data-end=\"287\">Factor IX activity test</strong> measures the <strong data-start=\"301\" data-end=\"321\">functional level</strong> of this protein in plasma.</p>\n<p data-start=\"827\" data-end=\"859\"><strong data-start=\"832\" data-end=\"859\">Low Factor IX Activity:</strong></p>\n<ol data-start=\"861\" data-end=\"1397\">\n<li data-start=\"861\" data-end=\"1166\">\n<p data-start=\"864\" data-end=\"901\"><strong data-start=\"864\" data-end=\"880\">Hemophilia B</strong> (Christmas disease):</p>\n<ul data-start=\"905\" data-end=\"1166\">\n<li data-start=\"905\" data-end=\"948\">\n<p data-start=\"907\" data-end=\"948\"><strong data-start=\"907\" data-end=\"948\">Inherited X-linked recessive disorder</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"952\" data-end=\"986\">\n<p data-start=\"954\" data-end=\"986\">Males affected, females carriers</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"990\" data-end=\"1166\">\n<p data-start=\"992\" data-end=\"1018\">Severity depends on level:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1024\" data-end=\"1166\">\n<li data-start=\"1024\" data-end=\"1060\">\n<p data-start=\"1026\" data-end=\"1060\">Severe (&lt;1%): spontaneous bleeding</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1066\" data-end=\"1112\">\n<p data-start=\"1068\" data-end=\"1112\">Moderate (1&ndash;5%): bleeding after minor trauma</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1118\" data-end=\"1166\">\n<p data-start=\"1120\" data-end=\"1166\">Mild (5&ndash;40%): bleeding after surgery or injury</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1168\" data-end=\"1397\">\n<p data-start=\"1171\" data-end=\"1205\"><strong data-start=\"1171\" data-end=\"1190\">Acquired causes</strong> (less common):</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1209\" data-end=\"1397\">\n<li data-start=\"1209\" data-end=\"1235\">\n<p data-start=\"1211\" data-end=\"1235\"><strong data-start=\"1211\" data-end=\"1235\">Vitamin K deficiency</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1239\" data-end=\"1258\">\n<p data-start=\"1241\" data-end=\"1258\"><strong data-start=\"1241\" data-end=\"1258\">Liver disease</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1262\" data-end=\"1312\">\n<p data-start=\"1264\" data-end=\"1312\"><strong data-start=\"1264\" data-end=\"1312\">Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation (DIC)</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1316\" data-end=\"1338\">\n<p data-start=\"1318\" data-end=\"1338\"><strong data-start=\"1318\" data-end=\"1338\">Warfarin therapy</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1342\" data-end=\"1397\">\n<p data-start=\"1344\" data-end=\"1397\">Presence of <strong data-start=\"1356\" data-end=\"1380\">Factor IX inhibitors</strong> (autoantibodies)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p data-start=\"1399\" data-end=\"1432\"><strong data-start=\"1404\" data-end=\"1432\">High Factor IX Activity:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1433\" data-end=\"1561\">\n<li data-start=\"1433\" data-end=\"1479\">\n<p data-start=\"1435\" data-end=\"1479\">Rare and usually not clinically significant.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1480\" data-end=\"1561\">\n<p data-start=\"1482\" data-end=\"1561\">May be associated with <strong data-start=\"1505\" data-end=\"1537\">increased risk of thrombosis</strong> in certain individuals.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1568\" data-end=\"1600\"><strong data-start=\"1572\" data-end=\"1600\">Supporting Lab Findings:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1602\" data-end=\"1727\">\n<li data-start=\"1602\" data-end=\"1622\">\n<p data-start=\"1604\" data-end=\"1622\"><strong data-start=\"1604\" data-end=\"1622\">Prolonged aPTT</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1623\" data-end=\"1638\">\n<p data-start=\"1625\" data-end=\"1638\"><strong data-start=\"1625\" data-end=\"1638\">Normal PT</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1639\" data-end=\"1727\">\n<p data-start=\"1641\" data-end=\"1727\">Mixing studies correct aPTT if deficiency is present, but not if inhibitor is present.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
